# Kernel configuration fragment for the ZTE ZXHN E2631 stage-1 image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL
#
# OpenWrt merges the kernel config from a list of files (include/target.mk,
# LINUX_KCONFIG_LIST) and applies the LAST one with full override power
# (scripts/kconfig.pl, config_add with mod_plus=0). The list ends with
# $(TOPDIR)/env/kernel-config, so a file at <tree>/env/kernel-config is the
# supported place to take something back out that a target config turned on.
#
# And there is nothing to take out except USB, so that is all this file does.
#
# WHAT IS BEING TAKEN OUT, AND WHY
#
# USB is removed from the kernel. Not deferred, not left as a module - removed.
#
# The sanechips target enables USB for the H3600, which has a socket on the
# panel: config-6.18 carries CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT=y, CONFIG_USB=m,
# CONFIG_USB_DWC3=m, CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=m and friends. On an E2631, reaching a
# USB controller is the one thing known to break the board: the controller is
# touched, the system hangs, the hardware watchdog restarts it, and it hangs
# again. A board in a reboot loop cannot be probed, so this has to be removed
# at the source rather than relied on to stay unused.
#
# The stock firmware's own kernel is the precedent, and it is why this fragment
# disables USB rather than disabling USB_SUPPORT as well. ZTE's kernel for this
# exact board has:
#
#     CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT=y
#     # CONFIG_USB is not set          <-- no host controller core at all
#
# That is: the menu is present, the code is not. It is also what OpenWrt's own
# generic config does (target/linux/generic/config-6.18 has both
# "# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set" and "# CONFIG_USB is not set"), so
# re-asserting it here restores the generic default instead of inventing a new
# one. With CONFIG_USB off, every controller driver loses its dependency and
# cascades off: DWC3, XHCI (both flavours), storage, the network drivers, the
# role switch, and USB_PCI, which only links HCDs to the PCI bus.
#
# This is one of three independent switches, and all three are off. Any one of
# them would be enough on its own; they are kept because each covers a
# different way USB could come back:
#
#   1. the board device tree leaves &usb at its inherited status = "disabled",
#      so no platform device is ever registered;
#   2. this file, so no USB code is built - a kmod cannot undo it, because a
#      module of a driver that is not there cannot be built;
#   3. the E2631 device fragment carries no USB kmod, so nothing can bind at
#      runtime. (The H3600 relies on DEVICE_PACKAGES for that; nothing does
#      here.)
#
# SCOPE - READ THIS BEFORE REUSING THE TREE
#
# env/kernel-config is tree-global, so this change applies to every device
# built from this checkout, not just the E2631. That is intentional here: the
# seed config builds only the E2631. If the H3600 is ever built from the same
# tree it will fail on its USB packages (kmod-usb3,
# kmod-usb-dwc3-generic-plat), and this file is the first thing to look at.
#
# TO RE-ENABLE USB, do not edit this file in a hurry. Two questions come first,
# and both need an answer that is not a device tree edit: whether the hang is
# gone (there is no evidence it is - a device tree change does not fix a
# driver), and which controller a socket is even wired to. The E2631's stock
# device tree marks both dwc2 at 0x09000000 and dwc3 at 0x09100000 "okay",
# which is not evidence that either is usable.

# The operative line: without a USB host controller core nothing can bind,
# built-in or modular. This mirrors the vendor kernel for this board.
# CONFIG_USB is not set

# Listed for the reader, and to hold the line if CONFIG_USB were ever turned
# back on: each of these is what would start poking the controllers. They are
# unreachable while CONFIG_USB is off, so kconfig will drop them.
# CONFIG_USB_COMMON is not set
# CONFIG_USB_DWC3 is not set
# CONFIG_USB_DWC3_HOST is not set
# CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD is not set
# CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PCI is not set
# CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PLATFORM is not set
# CONFIG_USB_STORAGE is not set
# CONFIG_USB_NET_DRIVERS is not set
# CONFIG_USB_ROLE_SWITCH is not set
# CONFIG_USB_PCI is not set
